THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
================================================================================

Office Kit bundles the following open-source components. Each is distributed
under its own license; the full license texts are included in the respective
package folders under resources/app/node_modules/ in the installed app (and in
node_modules/ of this repository after `npm install`).

The MIT License above does NOT apply to the office editor bundle
(vendor/office-editor/, below) or to the files in this repository that carry
an "SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later" or "AGPL-3.0-only" header:
the filex patches in patches/office-editor/ (AGPL-3.0-or-later) and the font
list generator in src/app/office-editor/fonts/ (AGPL-3.0-only with the
ONLYOFFICE additional terms, as it is derived from ONLYOFFICE core). Those are
licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License version 3, whose text is
in LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt; the ONLYOFFICE section 7 additional terms are in
LICENSES/ONLYOFFICE-additional-terms.txt. The rest of Office Kit stays MIT; it talks to the
office editor only through messages (a MessagePort) and a local file server.

- Office editor bundle — the in-app document, spreadsheet and presentation
  editing windows (vendor/office-editor/, built by
  scripts/build-office-editor.mjs from filex-office-editor v0.3.1)
  GNU Affero General Public License v3 (AGPL-3.0), NOT MIT. It contains:
  - ONLYOFFICE Docs Community Edition 9.4.0 (build 9.4.0.129) editor files
    (web-apps, sdkjs; source tag v9.4.0.129 of
    https://github.com/ONLYOFFICE/web-apps and https://github.com/ONLYOFFICE/sdkjs)
    Copyright (C) 2009-2026 Ascensio System SIA — AGPL-3.0 with the
    additional terms of its section 7 (vendor/office-editor/editor/LICENSE.txt);
    non-code content (illustrations, icon sets, documentation) is licensed
    under CC BY-SA 4.0. Office Kit ships a MODIFIED version (whole files left
    out; font list served from the user's installed fonts at run time): see
    vendor/office-editor/NOTICE-OfficeKit.md for the dated list of changes.
  - x2t, ONLYOFFICE's document converter, built to WebAssembly (release
    v9.4.0.129+2) from ONLYOFFICE core v9.4.0.129 (AGPL-3.0) with CryptPad's
    WebAssembly changes (AGPL-3.0-or-later) and BRF Tech's patches.
  - filex-office-editor (the app page and the bridge that answers the editor
    in place of a Document Server) — Copyright (C) 2026 BRF Tech —
    AGPL-3.0-or-later; its src/locks.ts is AGPL-3.0-only.
    https://github.com/BRF-Tech/filex-office-editor (commit 57dda3dae99a, tag
    v0.3.1); its LICENSE, NOTICE and editor/filex/CHANGES.txt are shipped in
    vendor/office-editor/.
  - third-party JavaScript inside the editor (Bootstrap, jQuery, RequireJS,
    Underscore, Backbone, Socket.IO and others) — MIT, BSD and Apache-2.0
    licenses, listed in vendor/office-editor/editor/3rd-Party.txt with their
    texts in vendor/office-editor/editor/license/.
  - third-party code compiled into the WebAssembly files (x2t.wasm and the
    sdkjs font/zlib engines: Boost, ICU, FreeType, HarfBuzz, Brotli, libpng,
    libjpeg, LibTIFF, OpenJPEG, JasPer, libxml2, Xpdf, DjVuLibre, Crypto++,
    the emscripten runtime and others) and the es6-promise and fetch
    polyfills — BSL-1.0, ICU, FTL, MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, IJG, GPL/LGPL and
    other licenses, with their notices in
    vendor/office-editor/THIRD-PARTY-NATIVE.txt (LICENSES/office-editor-third-
    party-native.txt in this repository).
  - the 14 URW++ base-14 Type 1 fonts (Nimbus Sans, Nimbus Roman, Nimbus
    Mono, Standard Symbols L, Dingbats) that ONLYOFFICE core embeds in x2t.wasm
    for PDF output — AGPL-3.0 with an exception allowing them to be embedded
    in PDF and PostScript documents. No other fonts are bundled: the editor
    reads the fonts installed on the PC.
  Corresponding Source: office-editor-source-<version>.zip, attached to each
  GitHub Release of Office Kit (made by scripts/make-office-source.mjs), plus
  the ONLYOFFICE sources at tag v9.4.0.129 named in its UPSTREAM.md.
  Details (in Korean): docs/LICENSES-OFFICE-EDITOR.md.

- rhwp (@rhwp/core) — HWP/HWPX engine (Rust/WebAssembly)
  Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Edward Kim — MIT License
  https://github.com/edwardkim/rhwp
  The Rust crates compiled into the WebAssembly module are listed, with their
  licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2/3-Clause, Zlib, ISC, Unicode, CC0 ...), in
  rhwp's THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md (shipped in resources/app/vendor/rhwp-studio/).

- rhwp-studio and @rhwp/editor — the in-app HWP/HWPX editor (web app built
  from rhwp tag v0.8.7, commit 1a76570e8339, by scripts/build-editor.mjs)
  Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Edward Kim — MIT License
  https://github.com/edwardkim/rhwp
  Shipped in resources/app/vendor/rhwp-studio/ and vendor/rhwp-editor-sdk/
  together with rhwp's LICENSE, THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md and VERSION.json.
  The bundled web app also contains:
  - CanvasKit (canvaskit-wasm, part of Skia) — BSD-3-Clause,
    Copyright (c) 2011 Google Inc.; full text in vendor/rhwp-studio/licenses/
  - @noble/hashes — MIT License, Paul Miller; full text in
    vendor/rhwp-studio/licenses/
  - small runtime helpers emitted by Vite — MIT License
  The rhwp-studio build tools (Vite, vite-plugin-pwa, Workbox — MIT) are used
  only at build time; the generated service worker and Workbox runtime are
  removed and are not shipped. Sample documents and web fonts are not shipped
  (if the editor is built with --with-fonts, only SIL OFL 1.1 / GUST licensed
  fonts are added, with their license files, under vendor/rhwp-studio/fonts/).

- Electron — MIT License, Copyright (c) Electron contributors / GitHub Inc.
  https://github.com/electron/electron
  (Electron bundles Chromium and Node.js; their licenses are shipped with the
  app as LICENSE.electron.txt and LICENSES.chromium.html.)

- @modelcontextprotocol/sdk — MIT License, Anthropic, PBC
  https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk

